on</span><span class="enc-snip">Erridupizir was a Gutian king who ruled in Mesopotamia in the 22nd century BCE, after the fall of the Akkadian Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/errol-barrow"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/errol-barrow.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Errol Barrow</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Errol Barrow was a Barbadian politician who founded the Democratic Labour Party and became premier of Barbados in 1961.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ershi"><span class="enc-name">Ershi</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ershi was the capital of Dayuan, the kingdom of the Ferghana valley in Central Asia known to Han China for its 'heavenly horses'.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/erythraean-sibyl"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/erythraean-sibyl.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Erythraean Sibyl</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">The Erythraean Sibyl was a legendary prophetess of Apollo associated with Erythrae, an Ionian city on the coast of Asia Minor opposite Chios.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/eryx"><span class="enc-name">Eryx</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Eryx was an ancient Elymian city on Mount Eryx in western Sicily, on the site of modern Erice.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/erzberg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/erzberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Erzberg</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Erzberg is a mountain near Eisenerz in Styria, Austria, made largely of siderite iron ore and mined since at least the Middle Ages.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/erzhu-rong"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/erzhu-rong.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Erzhu Rong</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Erzhu Rong was a frontier chieftain from northern Shanxi and a general of the Northern Wei dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/erzincan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/erzincan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Erzincan</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Erzincan is a city in eastern Turkey on the upper Euphrates, in a fertile plain surrounded by mountains.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/erzurum"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/erzurum.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Erzurum</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Erzurum is a city on a high plateau in eastern Turkey, near the sources of the Euphrates.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/esagila"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/esagila.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Esagila</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Esagila was the great temple of Marduk in Babylon, the most important sanctuary of the city.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/esarhaddon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/esarhaddon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Esarhaddon</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Esarhaddon was king of the Assyrian Empire in the seventh century BCE, the son of Sennacherib and father of Ashurbanipal.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/esau-de-buondelmonti"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/esau-de-buondelmonti.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Esau de' Buondelmonti</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Esau de' Buondelmonti was a Florentine nobleman who ruled Ioannina in Epirus from 1385 to 1411.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/escaldes-engordany"><span class="enc-name">Escaldes-Engordany</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Escaldes-Engordany is the seventh and newest parish of Andorra, separated from Andorra la Vella in 1978, with which it forms one continuous town.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/escaut-department"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/escaut-department.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Escaut (department)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Escaut was a department of the French Republic and Empire, formed in 1795 when France annexed the Austrian Netherlands.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/esch-sur-alzette"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/esch-sur-alzette.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Esch-sur-Alzette</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Esch-sur-Alzette is the second-largest city of Luxembourg, in the south of the country near the French border.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/eschen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eschen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Eschen</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Eschen is a municipality in the Unterland of Liechtenstein, on the slopes of the Eschnerberg.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/escher-wyss"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/escher-wyss.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Escher Wyss</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">Escher Wyss was a Swiss engineering company founded in Zurich in 1805 by Hans Caspar Escher and Salomon von Wyss, first as a cotton-spinning mill.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/eschiva-of-bures"><span class="enc-name">Eschiva of Bures</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Eschiva of Bures was Princess of Galilee in the crusader Kingdom of Jerusalem, heiress of the lordship through her family.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/eschnerberg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eschnerberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Eschnerberg</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Eschnerberg is a low, wooded ridge in the Unterland of Liechtenstein, rising above the Rhine valley.</span></a></li></ul>
